From 788acb1c47709ee490d36487b7051fa7f83c8228 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dlssg-to-xefg <dev@local>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:09:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Consolidate WMMA freeze/init fixes, .asi/.dll bridge
 coexistence, and safe Vulkan stub checks

1. D3D12->Vulkan WMMA bridge init, freeze & queue fixes (D3D12VulkanWmma.cpp, FrameGenerator.cpp):
   - Wrap XeFG::CreateContext + XeFG::Init on recorded xvk device in VkCommandBuffer +
     xvk::BeginRecording()/EndRecording() + vkQueueSubmit/vkQueueWaitIdle.
   - Cache failed ContextSettings so failed XeFG::Init never retries every frame.
   - Open xvk::BeginRecording() before copyInput() so pendingInit_ layout transitions flush first.
   - Pre-warm D3D12VulkanWmma::EnsureContext() inside FrameGenerator::CreateContext() so
     pipeline compilation never stalls Streamline's 500ms waitCPUFence deadline.
   - Fix PatchQueueVtable race condition and separate wrapped vs native shared fence / PostCopyRing.

2. Bulletproof .asi/.dll WMMA bridge bypass & Longshot-safe stub check (VulkanHost.h, VulkanHost.cpp):
   - Add thread-local VulkanHost::SetInternalBridgeBypass() RAII guard around D3D12VulkanWmma::Install
     alongside IsSelfModuleCaller + ignoredInstances tracking, so intermediate hooks (OptiScaler/overlays)
     can never expose the private WMMA bridge instance/device to VulkanHost.
   - Harden isUnsafeShortStub to verify >= 14 bytes of INT3/NOP padding after 6/9-byte loader dispatch
     stubs, preserving Vulkan Present Pacer on standard padded stubs while avoiding Longshot crashes.
